## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-model optimizations that preserve SLA and isolate tail latency in a multi-model serving setup.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-model caching for shared embeddings
- Per-model batching with HoLB isolation
- Cache sizing and eviction strategy
- Profiling and latency targeting

## Code Example
```javascript
// pseudo JS-like sketch; real impl would be in Python with TF Serving hooks
class LRUCache {
  constructor(cap) { this.cap = cap; this.map = new Map(); }
  get(k) { if (!this.map.has(k)) return null; const v = this.map.get(k); this.map.delete(k); this.map.set(k, v); return v; }
  put(k, v) { this.map.set(k, v); if (this.map.size > this.cap) { const first = this.map.keys().next().value; this.map.delete(first); } }
}
```
```python
from collections import OrderedDict
class LRUCache:
    def __init__(self, cap):
        self.cap = cap
        self.store = OrderedDict()
    def get(self, k):
        if k not in self.store: return None
        self.store.move_to_end(k)
        return self.store[k]
    def put(self, k, v):
        self.store[k] = v
        self.store.move_to_end(k)
        if len(self.store) > self.cap:
            self.store.popitem(last=False)
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure cache hit rate vs. latency impact?
- How would you handle cache coherence during model updates and embeddings drift?

## Why This Is Asked
